    <Mermaid id="cause_mapping_4"><![CDATA[
graph LR
    C1[Family and Peer Factors] --> D1[Dropping Out of High School]
    C2[Students Working Long Hours] --> D1
    C1 --> C2
    C1 --> C4
    C2 --> C1
    C3[Equitable School Funding] --> D1
    C3 --> C2
    C3 --> C4
    C4[ADHD Status] --> D1
    C5[School Finance Reform]-->C1
    C5-->C3

    style C1 fill:#e1f5ff
    style C2 fill:#e1f5ff
    style C3 fill:#e1f5ff
    style C4 fill:#e1f5ff
    style C5 fill:#e1f5ff
    style D1 fill:#fff4e1
]]>
   </Mermaid>

  <Vertical id="overview_of_connections_2">
    <SplitPanel id="comparison_4">
      <LeftPane>
         <Mermaid id="connection_4_diagram"><![CDATA[
graph LR
    C1[Family and Peer Factors]
    C5[School Finance Reform]-->C1

    style C1 fill:#e1f5ff
    style C5 fill:#e1f5ff
]]>
        </Mermaid>
      </LeftPane>
      <RightPane>
        <TextBlock id="factor_connection_4">
Changes to current school funding practices through school finance reforms will lead to more equitable money and resource allocations to schools in high-need districts allowing schools to be better able to serve those students who are at risk either because they work long hours or have ADHD.
        </TextBlock>
      </RightPane>
    </SplitPanel>
    <SplitPanel id="comparison_5">
      <LeftPane>
        <Mermaid id="connection_5_diagram"><![CDATA[
graph LR
    C3[Equitable School Funding]
    C5[School Finance Reform]-->C3

    style C3 fill:#e1f5ff
    style C5 fill:#e1f5ff
]]>
        </Mermaid>
      </LeftPane>
      <RightPane>
        <TextBlock id="factor_connection_5">
There are important family characteristics that directly benefit from increased school spending in the long run including adult wages, family income and reduced poverty rates. With greater family assets, students may feel less compelled to work long hours or will have resources to address their special needs.
        </TextBlock>
      </RightPane>
    </SplitPanel>
  </Vertical>

